    "created_at": "2022-02-10T22:37:14Z",
    "updated_at": "2022-02-10T22:37:14Z",
    "body": "The current version of the spec now explicitly mentions the possibility for multiple HID interfaces and defines the behavior for when the UA chooses to group HIDDevices:\r\n\r\n            If a device has multiple [=HID interfaces=], the dialog MAY present\r\n            only a single item that represents all the interfaces. When the\r\n            user selects an item that represents multiple [=HID interfaces=],\r\n            the user agent MUST grant access to all the [=HID interfaces=]\r\n            exposed by the device.\r\n\r\nI think there's more we can do in this area. For instance, providing a unique identifier for the device would enable script to detect when multiple HID interfaces are part of the same physical device. This could also be extended to other device APIs so script can detect when the same device is accessed through multiple APIs.",
    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
